[
{ type: upgrade
  maximum_version: 2.19.0
  message: <<EOM
Semaphore 2.19 dropped BoltDB support; the supported dialects are now mysql,
postgres and sqlite.  If your configuration still contains "dialect": "bolt",
the service will not start.

Do NOT simply change the dialect: semaphore would create an empty database
and all projects, templates, access keys and the task history would appear to
be gone.  The data is still in the BoltDB file and can be imported, but the
import tool only exists up to Semaphore 2.18:

  service semaphore stop
  cp /var/db/semaphore/database.boltdb /var/db/semaphore/database.boltdb.bak

  fetch -o /tmp/sem218.tar.gz https://github.com/semaphoreui/semaphore/releases/download/v2.18.29/semaphore_community_2.18.29_freebsd_amd64.tar.gz
  tar -xzf /tmp/sem218.tar.gz -C /tmp semaphore

Then set "dialect" to sqlite (or mysql/postgres) in
%%PREFIX%%/etc/semaphore/semaphore_config.json; a minimal example is installed
as %%PREFIX%%/etc/semaphore/config.json.sample.  The BoltDB file is only read
by the import, not modified:

  /tmp/semaphore migrate --from-boltdb /var/db/semaphore/database.boltdb --config %%PREFIX%%/etc/semaphore/semaphore_config.json
  semaphore migrate --config %%PREFIX%%/etc/semaphore/semaphore_config.json
  service semaphore start
  rm /tmp/semaphore

This update also restores the bundled web interface; earlier versions of the
port installed the API server only, so every UI route returned 404.

See the ports UPDATING entry of 20260826 for the same instructions, and
https://semaphoreui.com/docs/admin-guide/cli/migrations for the upstream
documentation of the import.
EOM
}
]
